      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea of sacrificing yourself for the \"good\" of the family sounds noble, but it's a dangerous myth. True love for your family doesn't demand your erasure; it demands your well-being. You are not a branch to be pruned; you are a living, breathing part of the whole, and your struggles do not negate your value. If you feel you are a burden, that feeling is a symptom of pain, not a factual truth about your worth.",
